# What NOT to upload to EAS Build.
#
# IMPORTANT: when this file exists, EAS uses it INSTEAD of .gitignore to decide
# what goes into the build archive. So everything secret or unnecessary has to
# be listed here explicitly — .gitignore is no longer consulted.
#
# Why this file exists: node_modules is committed to this repo (46k files,
# including 24 macOS/arm64 native binaries). Uploading a mac-built dependency
# tree to a Linux builder made the "Install dependencies" phase fail, and blew
# the archive up to 269 MB. EAS installs dependencies itself from
# package.json + package-lock.json, so the tree must not be shipped.

# Dependencies — EAS installs these on the builder, for the right platform
node_modules/

# Backend. Not part of the Expo app: nothing in server/ is imported by app/ or
# src/ (see server/README.md), and it vendors its own node_modules for Docker.
server/

# Design exploration + prototypes — HTML mockups, not app code
design-lab/
design-imports/
docs/

# Build output and local caches
dist/
.expo/
.test-build/
web-build/

# Secrets — never upload. EXPO_PUBLIC_* values come from eas.json `env` or
# EAS secrets, not from a local .env file.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
server/.env

# Local noise
.DS_Store
*.log
*.zip
ops/
paperclip_agents/
tests/
